  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "Evidence: The only completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) yields a low validation accuracy of ~48.5%, establishing a weak RNA-only baseline. The central design question for this multimodal cellular profiling study is whether adding image information meaningfully improves classification over RNA alone. Question tested: config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is a controlled extension of config_001 that adds only the image modality (resnet50) with the simplest fusion (concat), keeping the RNA encoder and profile setting identical. This directly isolates the contribution of image features. Why this is the best next experiment: With only one data point, the highest-uncertainty decision is whether the image modality is worth pursuing at all. A strong result here would justify investing remaining budget in multimodal variants (better encoders, multiprofile, transformer aggregation); a null result would redirect effort toward improving the RNA side (scvi, scgpt, multiprofile). This single experiment resolves the most consequential branching point in the search space under a limited budget."
}

